<urn:sc-runtime:qa:b-15:QA-001> qa:sprint "b-15" ;
  qa:severity "important" ;
  qa:reviewer "rust-qa-agent" ;
  qa:location "tests/integration/wizard/test_output_equivalence.py:149" ;
  qa:issue "The pinned-tree `just test` run fails two generated-project equivalence tests because the generated project's `lint` step returns `GEN.STEP_FAILED`: `test_stubbed_wizard_matches_var_file_tree` (line 149) and `test_different_var_files_produce_different_trees` (line 180). The run's generation suite reports 2 failures out of 74 tests." ;
  qa:remedy "Trace and correct the generated project's failing lint step or its generation-test invocation so both equivalence cases complete successfully, while retaining the wizard-versus-var-file tree comparison." ;
  qa:sourceCommit "e01c07bee0b5cde4e38ef8c129e1e06d3e3c7437" ;
  qa:status "open" .

<urn:sc-runtime:qa:b-18:qa1:QA-001>
  qa:id "QA-001" ;
  qa:sprint "b-18" ;
  qa:qaPass "qa-b-18-1" ;
  qa:severity "Important" ;
  qa:status "open" ;
  qa:reviewer "rust-qa-agent" ;
  qa:commit "e353c18c7441ab66e1061fae1c33cde3cc500225" ;
  qa:location "template/crates/daemon/src/main.rs:122" ;
  qa:issue "The runtime releases the instance lock before the generated application stops its cron worker. A new daemon can acquire the lock and start its own worker while the old worker is still running or draining, allowing overlapping execution of schedules." ;
  qa:recommendation "Ensure the instance lock remains held until the cron worker has stopped and joined, including startup-error paths. Add a regression that holds an old worker in flight during restart and proves the replacement cannot run until it drains." .
